ler names as strings instead of dictionaries.\n\nLet me structure the corrected tasks:\n\nFor Task 1: Install vault, I\'ll use ansible.builtin.apt with name and state. Then, notify the handlers as a list.\n\nFor Task 2 and 3, I\'ll use systemd with the appropriate actions.\n\nI think that should fix all the linting issues without changing the intended functionality.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: Install vault\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: "{{ vault_package }}"\n    state: present\n  notify:\n    - Daemon reload\n    - Restart vault\n\n- name: Daemon reload\n  ansible.systemd:\n    name: systemd\n    action: daemon-reload\n  become: true\n  tags: restarted\n\n- name: Restart vault\n  ansible.systemd:\n    name: vault\n    state: restarted\n  become: true\n  tags: restarted' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T05:12:01.232040322Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15194399205, 'load_duration': 98856245, 'prompt_eval_count': 2769, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1724565804, 'eval_count': 600, 'eval_duration': 13369371008, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--e9922d38-e6c1-4a1c-9ae4-93135d2d9113-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2769, 'output_tokens': 600, 'total_tokens': 3369}
