es.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with the correct module, parameters, and any conditions. I\'ll ensure that all tasks are in the correct order and that the YAML is valid.\n\nLet me double-check each task:\n\n1. Correct import_tasks for assert.yml.\n2. apt module for packages.\n3. lineinfile for GRUB_TIMEOUT, notify handler.\n4. lineinfile for GRUB_RECORDFAIL_TIMEOUT, notify handler.\n5. set_fact and lineinfile with conditionals.\n6. Conditional import_tasks.\n7. meta to flush handlers.\n\nI think that covers all the requirements. Now, I\'ll write the YAML accordingly, making sure there are no syntax errors.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  hosts: localhost\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Install required packages\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ grub_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set GRUB_TIMEOUT\n  lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/default/grub\n    regex: \'^GRUB_TIMEOUT=.*$\'\n    line: \'GRUB_TIMEOUT="{{ grub_timeout }}"\'\n    validate: true\n  notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Set GRUB_RECORDFAIL_TIMEOUT\n  lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/default/grub\n    regex: \'^GRUB_RECORDFAIL_TIMEOUT=.*$\'\n    line: \'GRUB_RECORDFAIL_TIMEOUT="{{ grub_recordfail_timeout }}"\'\n    validate: true\n  notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Add options to GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX\n  when: grub_options is defined and grub_options | list\n  set_fact:\n    grub_cmdline_options: "{{ grub_options | join(\',\') }}"\n  lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/default/grub\n    regex: \'(GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX=")(.*)("$)\'\n    line: \'\\1\\2 {{ grub_cmdline_options }}\n\'\n    validate: true\n  notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Import password.yml\n  import_tasks: password.yml\n  when: grub_set_password | default(\'false\') | bool\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta: flush_handlers\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T05:20:06.954969529Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 19515873221, 'load_dura