ce it\'s raw in Task 5, but here it\'s using the package module, I\'ll make sure to include the correct package name.\n\nTask 7 is gathering Ansible facts, which is done with the setup module. I\'ll add another setup task here to ensure facts are up to date after previous steps.\n\nTask 8 installs bootstrap packages using the package module. I\'ll use apt or yum based on the OS family, similar to Task 5 but using the package module instead of raw commands.\n\nI need to structure these tasks in the correct order. Task 1 imports assert.yml, then Task 2 waits for the port, followed by Task 3 preparing the system. If that fails, Task 4 rescues and gathers more facts. Then, Tasks 5 and 6 install packages, with 6 being conditional. After that, Task 7 gathers facts again, and finally, Task 8 installs packages properly.\n\nI should make sure each task has the correct parameters, especially for delegation, variables, and conditions. Also, the YAML must be valid, so proper indentation and syntax are crucial. I\'ll avoid any comments or explanations outside the YAML structure as per the instructions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Task 1: Import the assert.yml file for assertions\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  become: False\n\n- name: Task 2: Wait for a specified port to be available\n  wait_for:\n    port: "{{ bootstrap_port }}"\n    timeout: "{{ bootstrap_timeout }}"\n    state: started\n\n- name: Task 3: Prepare the system\n  setup:\n    gather_subset: all\n\n- name: Task 4: Gather additional facts if preparation encounters issues\n  fail:\n    msg: "Preparation failed, gathering additional facts"\n  rescue:\n    - name: Gather additional facts\n      import_tasks: facts.yml\n\n- name: Task 5: Install necessary bootstrap packages (raw)\n  raw: \n    cmd: "{{ package_manager_cmd }} install -y {{ bootstrap_packages }}"\n  when: ansible_os_family == "Debian" or ansible_distribution == "RedHat"\n\n- name: Task 6: Ensure libdnf5 is present on Fedora