content='<think>\nOkay, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. Let me go through each task and figure out how to translate them into YAML.\n\nStarting with Task 1: Remove Docker\'s apt key from trusted.gpg.d. I remember that the file is usually /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/docker.gpg. So, I\'ll use the file module with state=absent to delete it. I\'ll set path to that location and only if it exists, so the force parameter isn\'t needed here.\n\nNext, Task 2: Remove the old Docker source list. These files are in /etc/apt/sources.list.d/. The file is probably named something like docker.list. Again, using the file module with state=absent should work. I\'ll set the path to that file and make sure it\'s only removed if it exists.\n\nTask 3: Uninstall old Docker versions. Docker packages usually start with docker- or contain docker in their name. Using apt-get purge with the name pattern should remove them. I\'ll use the apt module with purge=true and name=docker*.\n\nTask 4: Remove the legacy repo file. I think this might be in /etc/docker.repo or similar. Using the file module again, set path to that location and state=absent.\n\nFor Task 5: Install dependencies. The required packages are apt-transport-https, ca-certificates, and python3-debian. I\'ll use the apt module with name set to these packages and state=installed.\n\nTask 6: Add or remove Docker repo based on a variable. If docker_add_repo is true, add the repo; else, remove it. I\'ll use the apt_repository module. When adding, I\'ll set repo to \'deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) ...\', but since it\'s a variable, I\'ll leave it as {{ docker_repository }}. When removing, state=absent. I\'ll make sure to notify the apt_update handler after this task.\n\nLastly, Task 7: Flush handlers to update apt cache immediately. This is done by calling meta: flush_handlers. I\'ll add a block with this meta directive.\n\nI need to structure each task correctly, ensuring the correct modules and parameters are used. Also, I have to make sure the playbook starts with --- and each task is properly indented in YAML. I\'ll avoid any hosts or vars sections since it\'s meant for an Ansible Role under tasks/main.yml.\n\nLet me review each task again to ensure I didn\'t miss any parameters. For example, in Task 3, I\'m using purge=true to remove all configurations as well. Also, in Task 6, I\'m using notify to trigger the handler, which should update the apt cache after the repo is added or removed.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now, I\'ll write the YAML playbook accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Ensure apt key is not present in trusted.gpg.d\n  file:\n    path: /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/docker.gpg\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Ensure old apt source list is not present in /etc/apt/sources.list.d\n  file:\n    path: /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Ensure old versions of Docker are not installed\n  apt:\n    name: docker*\n    state: purge\n\n- name: Ensure legacy repo file is not present\n  file:\n    path: /etc/docker.repo\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Ensure dependencies are installed\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: installed\n  with_items:\n    - apt-transport-https\n    - ca-certificates\n    - python3-debian\n\n- name: Add or remove Docker repository\n  apt_repository:\n    repo: "{{ docker_repository }}"\n    state: "{{ \'present\' if docker_add_repo else \'absent\' }}"\n  notify: apt update cache\n\n- name: Ensure handlers are notified immediately to update the apt cache\n  meta: flush_handlers\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T05:33:13.940447089Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 16184820694, 'load_duration': 105755213, 'prompt_eval_count': 489, 'prompt_eval_duration': 140023146, 'eval_count': 836, 'eval_duration': 15937699340, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--132f9e20-effb-4cdf-a864-586d2a13a990-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 489, 'output_tokens': 836, 'total_tokens': 1325}
