tions are met. Also, make sure each task has the correct modules and arguments, and that handlers are notified properly.\n\nPotential issues to watch for: correct OS detection, version checks, and proper inclusion of task files. Also, ensuring that the playbook starts with \'---\' and is valid YAML.\n\nI think the final playbook should be a list of tasks, each with the appropriate module, args, and conditions. Each task should be under a \'tasks\' key in the playbook, without any hosts or vars at the top.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Load OS-specific vars\n  include_vars:\n    file: "{{ distribution|lower }}/os_vars.yml" \n      vars_files:\n        - "{{ os_family }}.yml"\n\n- name: Include RedHat-specific setup tasks\n  include_tasks: setup-RedHat.yml\n  when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat"\n\n- name: Include Debian-specific setup tasks\n  include_tasks: setup-Debian.yml\n  when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n\n- name: Install Docker packages\n  when: (ansible_version >= "2.12" or ansible_os_family not in ["RedHat", "Debian"]) is false\n  include_tasks: install-docker.yml\n\n- name: Install Docker packages (with downgrade option)\n  when: (ansible_version >= "2.12" and ansible_os_family in ["RedHat", "Debian"])\n  include_tasks: install-docker-with-downgrade.yml\n\n- name: Install docker-compose plugin\n  when: (ansible_version >= "2.12" or ansible_os_family not in ["RedHat", "Debian"]) is false\n  and docker_install_compose_plugin is true\n  include_tasks: install-docker-compose-plugin.yml\n\n- name: Install docker-compose-plugin (with downgrade option)\n  when: (ansible_version >= "2.12" and ansible_os_family in ["RedHat", "Debian"]) \n  and docker_install_compose_plugin is true\n  include_tasks: install-docker-compose-plugin-with-downgrade.yml\n\n- name: Ensure /etc/docker/ directory exists\n  when: docker_daemon_options is defined\n  file:\n    path: /etc/docker\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Configure Docker daemon options\n  when: doc