content="<think>\nOkay, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the user's instructions. Let me go through each task step by step to make sure I don't miss anything.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with '---' on the first line. That's straightforward. I'll make sure to include that.\n\nNext, the structure has to be valid YAML, conforming to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. I'll need to ensure proper indentation and syntax in each task.\n\nThe tasks should be structured so they can be part of an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory, specifically tasks/main.yml. So, I'll write each task as a list under the main.yml file.\n\nLet's look at each task:\n\nTask 1: Check if Helm binary exists. I'll use the shell module to check if 'helm' is present in '/usr/local/bin/helm'. The command 'which helm' should return the path if it exists. I'll set the register variable to 'helm_exists' to capture the result.\n\nTask 2: Check Helm version. This should only happen if Task 1 passes. I'll use the shell module again, but only when 'helm_exists' is true. The command 'helm version --short' will get the version, and I'll register it to 'helm_version'.\n\nTask 3: Download Helm if the binary doesn't exist or if the version is outdated. Here, I'll use the get_url module to download the latest stable Helm binary. The url should point to the latest version, which I can construct using the version from Task 2. I'll download it to '/tmp/helm.tar.gz' and set the correct permissions.\n\nTask 4: Copy the Helm binary. Again, this depends on Task 3 succeeding. I'll extract the tar.gz file and move it to '/usr/local/bin/helm'. I'll set the correct permissions and use the file module to ensure it's in place.\n\nI need to make sure each task has the correct conditionals (when:). Also, the order of tasks is crucial: check existence, then version, then download if needed, then copy.\n\nI'll structure each task with the correct modules and arguments. For the shell commands, I'll use the appropriate arguments for exit codes and capturing output.\n\nI should avoid any unnecessary comments or explanations, just the YAML code as required.\n\nPutting it all together, I'll write each task in order, ensuring proper indentation and that each task only runs when its condition is met. This should result in a valid Ansible Playbook that meets all the specified requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if Helm binary exists\n  shell: which helm\n  args:\n    chdir: /usr/local/bin\n  register: helm_exists\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Check Helm version\n  shell: helm version --short\n  args:\n    chdir: /usr/local/bin\n  register: helm_version\n  when: helm_exists.rc == 0\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Download helm\n  get_url:\n    url: https://get.helm.sh/helm-{{ helm_version.stdout }}-linux-amd64.tar.gz\n    dest: /tmp/helm.tar.gz\n    mode: 0755\n  when: helm_exists.rc != 0 or helm_version.rc != 0\n\n- name: Copy helm binary into place\n  shell: mv /tmp/linux-amd64/helm /usr/local/bin/helm && chmod 755 /usr/local/bin/helm\n  args:\n    chdir: /tmp\n  when: helm_exists.rc != 0 or helm_version.rc != 0\n  changed_when: false\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T06:04:23.671173961Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15373558526, 'load_duration': 84577076, 'prompt_eval_count': 353, 'prompt_eval_duration': 104179708, 'eval_count': 773, 'eval_duration': 15183414616, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--4e910cc8-12be-4b04-83fc-22bf6f779aaa-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 353, 'output_tokens': 773, 'total_tokens': 1126}
