ces at the end of lines to prevent the \'trailing-spaces\' error.\n\nFinally, I\'ll ensure that all task names, variables, and module calls remain exactly as in the original playbook to maintain the intended functionality.\n\nBy systematically addressing each error message and ensuring proper YAML syntax, the playbook should now pass yamllint and ansible-lint checks without altering its operational intent.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create ssl key\n  openssl_privatekey:\n    path: "{{ ssl_key_path }}/{{ item.key }}"\n    provider: rsa\n    size: 2048\n  register: ssl_key_result\n  when: item.key is not None\n  loop:\n    - {key: \'server1\'}\n    - {key: \'server2\'}\n\n- name: Set permissions for private key\n  file:\n    path: "{{ ssl_key_path }}/{{ item.key }}"\n    mode: 0604\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n  when: item.key is not None\n  loop:\n    - {key: \'server1\'}\n    - {key: \'server2\'}\n\n- name: Create ssl csr\n  openssl_csr:\n    path: "{{ ssl_csr_path }}/{{ item.key }}.csr"\n    privatekey_path: "{{ ssl_key_path }}/{{ item.key }}"\n    common_name: "{{ item.cn }}"\n    subject_alt_names: [\'DNS:{{ item.key }}\']\n  register: ssl_csr_result\n  when: item.key is not None\n  loop:\n    - {key: \'server1\', cn: \'Server1\'}\n    - {key: \'server2\', cn: \'Server2\'}\n\n- name: Set permissions for csr\n  file:\n    path: "{{ ssl_csr_path }}/{{ item.key }}.csr"\n    mode: 0604\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n  when: item.key is not None\n  loop:\n    - {key: \'server1\'}\n    - {key: \'server2\'}\n\n- name: Create ssl certificates\n  openssl_certificate:\n    path: "{{ ssl_cert_path }}/{{ item.key }}.crt"\n    csr_path: "{{ ssl_csr_path }}/{{ item.key }}.csr"\n    privatekey_path: "{{ ssl_key_path }}/{{ item.key }}"\n    signing.cert: /path/to/ca/cert.pem\n    signing.key: /path/to/ca/key.pem\n    signing.algorithm: sha256\n  register: ssl_cert_result\n  when: item.key is not None\n  loop:\n    - {key: \'server1\'}\n    - {key: \'server2\'}\