en\' clause is written without proper syntax. Let me check the YAML structure.\n\nWait, no, the \'when\' clause is correctly indented. So the issue must be that the \'controller_node\' is not a boolean. To fix this, perhaps we should ensure that \'controller_node\' is treated as a boolean. Alternatively, we can cast it in the \'when\' clause.\n\nBut since the user didn\'t mention changing variables, perhaps the fix is to adjust the \'when\' clause to ensure it\'s a boolean.\n\nAnother approach is to simplify the \'when\' clause. For example, instead of checking if ansible_distribution is in multiple lists, we can combine them into a single list.\n\nWait, in the playbook, the \'when\' clause for the \'Download promtail binaries to controller node\' task is:\n\nwhen: (ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\'] or ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']) and controller_node\n\nThis can be simplified to:\n\nwhen: ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\', \'debian\', \'ubuntu\'] and controller_node\n\nThis might make the condition clearer and ensure it\'s a boolean.\n\nBut the main issue is the \'truthy\' error. So perhaps the \'controller_node\' is a string, and we need to cast it to a boolean in the \'when\' clause.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the \'when\' clause is written as a string without proper evaluation. For example, if it\'s written as a string like \'true\' instead of a boolean.\n\nWait, looking at the original playbook, the \'when\' clause is correctly using boolean logic. So perhaps the issue is that the line is too long, which is another error mentioned.\n\nLine 24 is too long. Let me check that line.\n\nLine 24 in the original playbook is:\n\nwhen: (ansible_distribution == \'debian\' or ansible_distribution == \'ubuntu\')\n\nThis is part of the first \'Ensure the unzip package is available\' task using apt. The line is 106 characters long, which exceeds the 80 character limit.\n\nSo to fix this, I need to break the line into multiple lines, perhaps using YAML\'s line continuation with backslashes or parentheses.\n\nIn YAML, you can break a line by putting the condition in parentheses and continuing on the next line.\n\nSo, for line 24, the \'when\' condition can be rewritten as:\n\nwhen: (ansible_distribution == \'debian\'\n       or ansible_distribution == \'ubuntu\')\n\nThis way, the line doesn\'t exceed 80 characters.\n\nSimilarly, for line 30, the \'when\' condition is:\n\nwhen: (ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\'] or ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']) and controller_node\n\nThis is also a long line and might be causing the truthy error. Let me break it into multiple lines for clarity and to fit within 80 characters.\n\nSo, I\'ll rewrite it as:\n\nwhen: (ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\']\n       or ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']) and controller_node\n\nBut wait, the error is about truthy values, so perhaps the \'when\' clause is not correctly structured. Alternatively, maybe the \'controller_node\' is not a boolean. To ensure it\'s a boolean, perhaps we can cast it using \'ansible_boolean\' filter.\n\nBut the user didn\'t mention changing variables, so perhaps the main fixes are:\n\n1. Break long lines into multiple lines to adhere to the 80 character limit.\n2. Ensure that \'when\' conditions are properly structured as boolean expressions.\n\nAdditionally, looking at lines 30, 38, 111, and 120, the \'when\' conditions are using \'ansible_distribution in [...]\' which is correct, but the line length is causing issues. By breaking these lines, we can fix the line length and possibly the truthy errors.\n\nSo, the plan is:\n\n- For each task with a long \'when\' condition, break the line into multiple lines using YAML\'s line continuation.\n- Ensure that all \'when\' conditions are properly structured as boolean expressions to avoid truthy value errors.\n\nNow, let me apply these changes to the playbook.\n\nFirst task (line 24):\n\nOriginal \'when\' condition:\nwhen: ansible_distribution == \'debian\' or ansible_distribution == \'ubuntu\'\n\nRewrite as:\nwhen: (ansible_distribution == \'debian\'\n       or ansible_distribution == \'ubuntu\')\n\nSimilarly, for the \'yum\' task (line 30):\n\nOriginal \'when\' condition:\nwhen: ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\'] or ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\'] and controller_node\n\nRewrite as:\nwhen: (ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\']\n       or ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']) and controller_node\n\nWait, but in YAML, the \'and\' has higher precedence than \'or\', so the condition might not be as intended. To be safe, perhaps wrap the entire condition in parentheses.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the \'when\' condition can be simplified by combining the distributions into a single list.\n\nBut for now, the main fix is to break the lines.\n\nNext, the task \'Download promtail binaries to controller node\' has a \'when\' condition that\'s too long. Let\'s break it.\n\nOriginal \'when\' condition:\nwhen: (ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\'] or ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']) and controller_node\n\nRewrite as:\nwhen: (ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\']\n       or ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']) and controller_node\n\nSimilarly, for the task \'Propagate promtail binaries\', the \'when\' condition is:\n\nwhen: promtail_dist == \'remote\'\n\nWhich is fine, but perhaps it\'s a long line, so break it if necessary.\n\nWait, the error was on line 111 and 120, which correspond to other \'when\' conditions. Let me check.\n\nLooking back, the error messages were:\n\n30:13: truthy value should be one of [false, true] (truthy)\n38:13: same\n111:17: same\n120:17: same\n\nWait, line 38 is another \'when\' condition. Let me check what\'s on line 38.\n\nLooking at the original playbook, line 38 is the \'Propagate locally distributed promtail archive\' task, which has a \'when\' condition:\n\nwhen: (not promtail_binary_exists.stat.exists and promtail_dist == \'local\')\n\nThis is a valid condition, but perhaps the line is too long. Let me break it.\n\nSo, rewrite as:\n\nwhen: (not promtail_binary_exists.stat.exists\n       and promtail_dist == \'local\')\n\nSimilarly, for line 111 and 120, which are other \'when\' conditions, I\'ll break them into multiple lines.\n\nFor example, line 111 might be the \'Propagate promtail binaries\' task:\n\nwhen: promtail_dist == \'remote\'\n\nWhich is fine, but perhaps the line is too long, so break it.\n\nFinally, line 120 is the \'Start and enable promtail service\' task, which doesn\'t have a \'when\' condition, so perhaps that\'s not the issue. Wait, no, the error is on line 120, which is the \'systemd\' task. Let me check.\n\nWait, in the original playbook, the last task is \'Start and enable promtail service\' without a \'when\' condition. So perhaps the error is elsewhere. Maybe the \'when\' condition in another task.\n\nWait, perhaps I miscounted the lines. Let me recount the lines in the original playbook.\n\nBut regardless, the main fixes are:\n\n1. Break all long \'when\' conditions into multiple lines to adhere to the 80 character limit.\n2. Ensure that \'when\' conditions are properly structured as boolean expressions to avoid truthy value errors.\n\nBy making these changes, the yamllint errors should be resolved without altering the functional intent of the playbook.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Ensure the unzip package is available on the target system\n  apt:\n    name: unzip\n    state: present\n    update_cache: true\n  become: true\n  changed_when: false\n  run_once: true\n  vars:\n    ansible_pkg_mgr: apt\n  when: (ansible_distribution == \'debian\'\n        or ansible_distribution == \'ubuntu\')\n\n- name: Ensure the unzip package is available on the target system\n  yum:\n    name: unzip\n    state: present\n    update_cache: true\n  become: true\n  changed_when: false\n  run_once: true\n  vars:\n    ansible_pkg_mgr: yum\n  when: (ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\']\n        or ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']) and controller_node\n\n- name: Create a system group for promtail\n  group:\n    name: promtail\n    state: present\n    system: yes\n    gid: null\n  become: true\n\n- name: Create the promtail user\n  user:\n    name: promtail\n    state: present\n    system: yes\n    group: promtail\n    shell: /sbin/nologin\n    home: /nonexistent\n    create_home: false\n  become: true\n\n- name: Ensure the /usr/local/bin directory exists\n  file:\n    path: /usr/local/bin\n    state: directory\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  become: true\n\n- name: Create config directories\n  file:\n    path: "{{ item }}"\n    state: directory\n    mode: \'0755\'\n    owner: promtail\n    group: promtail\n  become: true\n  loop:\n    - /etc/promtail\n    - /var/lib/promtail\n\n- name: Create application directories\n  file:\n    path: "{{ item }}"\n    state: directory\n    mode: \'0755\'\n    owner: promtail\n    group: promtail\n  become: true\n  loop:\n    - /opt/promtail\n\n- name: Check if the promtail binary exists\n  stat:\n    path: /usr/local/bin/promtail\n  register: promtail_binary_exists\n\n- name: Download promtail binaries\n  get_url:\n    url: "{{ promtail_url }}"\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/promtail.tgz\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  become: true\n  when: (not promtail_binary_exists.stat.exists\n        and promtail_dist == \'remote\')\n\n- name: Propagate locally distributed promtail archive\n  copy:\n    src: "{{ promtail_local_archive }}"\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/promtail.tgz\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  become: true\n  when: (not promtail_binary_exists.stat.exists\n        and promtail_dist == \'local\')\n\n- name: Download promtail binaries to controller node\n  get_url:\n    url: "{{ promtail_controller_url }}"\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/promtail.tgz\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  become: true\n  when: (ansible_distribution in [\'centos\', \'rhel\', \'ol\']\n        or ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']) and controller_node\n\n- name: Propagate promtail binaries\n  copy:\n    src: /usr/local/bin/promtail.tgz\n    dest: "{{ promtail_binary_dir }}/promtail.tgz"\n    remote_src: yes\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  become: true\n  when: promtail_dist == \'remote\'\n\n- name: Unpack promtail binaries\n  unarchive:\n    src: /usr/local/bin/promtail.tgz\n    dest: /opt/promtail\n    remote_src: yes\n    owner: promtail\n    group: promtail\n    mode: \'0755\'\n    nofail: true\n  become: true\n\n- name: Create symlink to latest version\n  file:\n    path: /usr/local/bin/promtail\n    state: link\n    src: /opt/promtail/./bin/promtail\n  become: true\n\n- name: Write configuration\n  template:\n    src: promtail-config.j2\n    dest: /etc/promtail/promtail.yml\n    owner: promtail\n    group: promtail\n    mode: \'0644\'\n  become: true\n\n- name: Create systemd service unit\n  template:\n    src: promtail-service.j2\n    dest: /etc/systemd/system/promtail.service\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: \'0644\'\n  become: true\n\n- name: Start and enable promtail service\n  systemd:\n    name: promtail\n    state: started\n    enabled: true\n  become: true\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T06:30:07.539120988Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 83713493317, 'load_duration': 86055268, 'prompt_eval_count': 1975, 'prompt_eval_duration': 398983588, 'eval_count': 3673, 'eval_duration': 83226924718, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--4c703e57-0f97-4256-b01c-427b4c55a5af-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1975, 'output_tokens': 3673, 'total_tokens': 5648}
