e no extra headers like hosts or vars, as they\'re not needed in a role\'s tasks/main.yml file.\n\nI\'ll double-check that all tasks are in the correct order and that the module names and parameters match exactly what\'s specified. Using the correct YAML formatting, I\'ll ensure the playbook is valid and can be included directly in an Ansible Role without issues.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the playbook to make sure it adheres to yamllint and ansible-lint standards, removing any unnecessary comments or explanations as per the user\'s instructions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Install python pip\n  apt:\n    name: python-pip\n    state: present\n\n- name: Configure pip proxy\n  template:\n    src: pip.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/pip.conf\n  when: python_pip_proxy is defined\n\n- name: Trust hosts\n  template:\n    src: pip.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/pip.conf\n  when: python_pip_trusted_host is defined\n\n- name: Update pip\n  pip:\n    name: pip\n    state: present\n    extra_args: --upgrade\n  when:\n    - python_pip_update\n    - distribution_release is not in [\'bookworm\', \'noble\']\n    - ansible_os_family != \'Alpine\'\n\n- name: Install requested modules\n  pip:\n    name: "{{ item.name }}"\n    version: "{{ item.version | default(\'latest\') }}"\n    state: "{{ item.state | default(\'present\') }}"\n  loop: "{{ python_pip_modules | default([]) | list }}"\n  when:\n    - python_pip_modules is defined\n    - distribution_release is not in [\'bookworm\', \'noble\']\n    - ansible_os_family != \'Alpine\'\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T06:32:31.896038736Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13975128572, 'load_duration': 90939810, 'prompt_eval_count': 510, 'prompt_eval_duration': 108109185, 'eval_count': 821, 'eval_duration': 13774980511, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--