 over `httpd_locations` would make sense.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll adjust the `template` task. I\'ll remove the `vars` section and instead use `with_vars` to include the `httpd_locations` variable. Additionally, I\'ll add a `loop` to handle each location, ensuring that the template correctly processes each item.\n\nSo, the corrected task should look like this: use `ansible.builtin.template` with `src` and `dest`, set `mode: \'0644\'`, include the `httpd_locations` variable, and loop through each location to apply the configuration.\n\nI also notice that the `a2enmod` module is being used, but ansible-lint warns about another version being found. However, since the user instructed not to alter the module unless necessary, I\'ll leave it as is.\n\nFinally, I\'ll structure the YAML correctly, ensuring proper indentation and formatting to avoid any syntax errors that might cause further issues.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Enable proxy and proxy_http modules on Debian and Suse systems\n  ansible.debian.a2enmod:\n    module: "{{ item }}"\n    state: enabled\n  loop:\n    - proxy\n    - proxy_http\n  become: true\n  notify:\n    - httpd-restart\n\n- name: Configure locations using a template\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: location.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/apache2/sites-available/location.conf\n    mode: \'0644\'\n  with_vars:\n    httpd_locations: "{{ httpd_locations }}"\n  notify:\n    - httpd-configtest\n    - httpd-restart\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T06:35:03.630217411Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 22082650263, 'load_duration': 94984335, 'prompt_eval_count': 5738, 'prompt_eval_duration': 4434822491, 'eval_count': 801, 'eval_duration': 17551717957, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--2f3e3e46-a945-4367-ab84-847b7fa002d7-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5738, 'output_tokens': 801, 'total_tokens': 6539}
