config_test\n  when: "ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']"\n\nThat seems correct. The \'when\' is a string, which is acceptable.\n\nWait, maybe the issue is with the \'when\' condition in another task. Let me check the \'Import ssl.yml\' task. It\'s \'when: https_ssl_enable\'. If \'https_ssl_enable\' is a variable that\'s set to a truthy value like \'yes\' or \'true\', that\'s fine. But if it\'s a string, perhaps it\'s causing an issue. But in the playbook, it\'s just a variable, so it\'s correct.\n\nWait, perhaps the problem is with the \'file\' module in the \'Removing default html\' task. The \'state\' is \'absent\', which is correct.\n\nWait, I think the main issues are:\n\n1. Using \'yes\' instead of \'true\' in the \'flush_handlers\' task.\n2. Missing a newline at the end of the file.\n\nSo to fix the first issue, change \'flush_handlers: yes\' to \'flush_handlers: true\'. \n\nFor the second issue, ensure that the YAML file ends with a newline. So after the last task, add a blank line or make sure the last line ends correctly.\n\nLet me go through the playbook and make these changes.\n\nIn the \'Flush handlers\' task, change \'flush_handlers: yes\' to \'flush_handlers: true\'.\n\nAlso, ensure that the file ends with a newline. So after the last task, there should be a blank line.\n\nWait, but in the original playbook, the last task is \'Start and enable httpd\', which ends with \'enabled: yes\'. So that\'s correct. The issue is with the \'flush_handlers\' task.\n\nSo the corrected \'Flush handlers\' task should have \'flush_handlers: true\'.\n\nLet me write out the corrected playbook with these changes.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  run_once: true\n  host: localhost\n\n- name: Install apache httpd\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ httpd_packages }}"\n    state: present\n  when: "ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']"\n\n- name: Configure selinux\n  become: true\n  command: setsebool -P httpd_can_connect_db 1\n  when: ansible_is_selinux_enabled\n\n- name: Configure selinux ports\n  become: true\n  command: setsebool -P httpd_talk_to_self 1\n  when: ansible_is_selinux_enabled\n\n- name: Configure httpd\n  template:\n    src: "{{ httpd_config_src }}"\n    dest: "{{ httpd_config_dest }}"\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: httpd_config_test\n\n- name: Activate httpd module | Debian\n  command: a2enmod "{{ item }}"\n  with_items: "{{ httpd_modules }}"\n  notify: httpd_config_test\n  when: "ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']"\n\n- name: Import ssl.yml\n  import_tasks: ssl.yml\n  when: https_ssl_enable\n\n- name: Import locations.yml\n  import_tasks: locations.yml\n  when: "httpd_locations is defined"\n\n- name: Import vhosts.yml\n  import_tasks: vhosts.yml\n  when: "httpd_vhosts is defined"\n\n- name: Configure ports\n  template:\n    src: "{{ httpd_ports_src }}"\n    dest: "{{ httpd_ports_dest }}"\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: httpd_config_test\n  when: "ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'suse\']"\n\n- name: Import directories.yml\n  import_tasks: directories.yml\n  when: "httpd_directories is defined"\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  flush_handlers: true\n\n- name: Removing default html\n  file:\n    path: "{{ httpd_data_dir }}/index.html"\n    state: absent\n  when: httpd_remove_example\n\n- name: Start and enable httpd\n  service:\n    name: apache2\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T06:41:07.685218388Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 40650555555, 'load_duration': 93146621, 'prompt_eval_count': 1279, 'prompt_eval_duration': 403065807, 'eval_count': 1815, 'eval_duration': 40153156356, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--dcdf4162-278f-4cdc-a639-6e5dac9f1ca2-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1279, 'output_tokens': 1815, 'total_tokens': 3094} 46%|████▌     | 46/100 [1:45:18<2:23:57, 159.96s/it]
