l import_file task is the issue. Let me look at that.\n\nThe first task is:\n\n- import_file:\n    file: ./assert.yml\n    state: present\n\nBut in Ansible, the import_file is a module, so it should be under a task with a name.\n\nSo the correct structure should be:\n\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_file:\n    file: ./assert.yml\n    state: present\n\nSo the \'import_file\' module should be under a task with a \'name\' field.\n\nIn the faulty playbook, the first task is missing the \'name\' field, which is causing the syntax error because it\'s a list item without a proper structure.\n\nTherefore, the first task is incorrectly written as a list item without a \'name\' and module structure.\n\nSo to fix this, I\'ll add the \'name\' field to each task, ensuring that each task is a dictionary with \'name\' and the module.\n\nSo, the corrected playbook should have each task starting with \'- name: Task name\' followed by the module and parameters.\n\nLet me reconstruct the playbook accordingly.\n\nThe corrected playbook will start with ---, then each task as a list item with name and module, properly indented.\n\nSo the fixed playbook should look like this:\n\n---\n\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_file:\n    file: ./assert.yml\n    state: present\n\n- name: Enable redis module stream (RHEL 8)\n  dnf:\n    name: redis\n    state: enabled\n    list: module\n\n- name: Install redis\n  package:\n    name: \'{{ redis_packages }}\'\n    state: present\n\n- name: Configure redis\n  template:\n    src: redis.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/redis.conf\n    mode: 0644\n    owner: redis\n    group: redis\n  notify: restart redis service\n\n- name: Start and enable redis\n  service:\n    name: \'{{ redis_service }}\'\n    state: started\n    enabled: true\n\nThis structure ensures that each task is a dictionary under a list, with proper \'name\' fields and modules, fixing the syntax error reported by yamllint.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_file:\n    file: ./assert.yml\n    state: present\n\n- name: Enable redis module stream (RHEL 8)\n  dnf:\n    name: redis\n    state: enabled\n    list: module\n\n- name: Install redis\n  package:\n    name: \'{{ redis_packages }}\'\n    state: present\n\n- name: Configure redis\n  template:\n    src: redis.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/redis.conf\n    mode: 0644\n    owner: redis\n    group: redis\n  notify: restart redis service\n\n- name: Start and enable redis\n  service:\n    name: \'{{ redis_service }}\'\n    state: started\n    enabled: true' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T06:47:56.229765467Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 45124896687, 'load_duration': 83887745, 'prompt_eval_count': 652, 'prompt_eval_duration': 411209502, 'eval_count': 2028, 'eval_duration': 44628831506, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--6fd7bfb3-120c-456b-8259-9f2f7786e570-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 652, 'output_tokens': 2028, 'total_tokens': 2680}
