tions.\n\nI also need to ensure that the playbook is valid for inclusion in an Ansible Role under the tasks directory, so I won\'t include any playbook-level directives like `hosts:` or `vars:`.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the playbook to make sure it correctly enables the modules, copies the template, sets permissions, and notifies the necessary handlers. That should meet all the user\'s requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Enable proxy modules in Apache\n  ansible.builtin.shell: a2enmod proxy proxy_http\n  args:\n    chdir: /etc/apache2/mods-enabled\n\n- name: Configure Apache locations using a template\n  ansible.apache2.template:\n    src: "templates/apache-proxy.conf.j2"\n    dest: /etc/apache2/sites-available/apache-proxy.conf\n    group: root\n    mode: 644\n    owner: root\n  notify: \n    - test_apache_config\n    - restart_apache\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T07:05:01.898924861Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13665903840, 'load_duration': 79127280, 'prompt_eval_count': 327, 'prompt_eval_duration': 97490339, 'eval_count': 636, 'eval_duration': 13487960909, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--f68d9f05-71e3-43bb-86bb-125afc73c434-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 327, 'output_tokens': 636, 'total_tokens': 963}
