AML syntax is correct. Using a list for the module parameter should be properly formatted with commas and enclosed in brackets.\n\nSo, the corrected Task 1 will have one ansible.builtin.apache_module with module set to a list containing \'proxy\' and \'proxy_http\'. This should fix the duplication issue and keep the playbook functional.\n\nI think that\'s all. I\'ll make sure the playbook starts with --- and each task is correctly indented. No other changes are needed since the rest of the playbook is valid.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Enable proxy modules in Apache\n  ansible.builtin.apache_module:\n    state: enabled\n    module:\n      - proxy\n      - proxy_http\n\n- name: Configure Apache locations using a template\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: "templates/apache-proxy.conf.j2"\n    dest: /etc/apache2/sites-available/apache-proxy.conf\n    group: root\n    mode: "0644"\n    owner: root\n  notify:\n    - test_apache_config\n    - restart_apache\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T07:05:47.524149122Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13013578976, 'load_duration': 86942668, 'prompt_eval_count': 527, 'prompt_eval_duration': 151802251, 'eval_count': 644, 'eval_duration': 12773748162, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--6ad5bf11-a602-4c86-bd51-7666fd430eda-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 527, 'output_tokens': 644, 'total_tokens': 1171}
