th an \'if\' condition in the command string, checking if rke2_type is not \'server\'.\n\nTasks 9 and 10 are wait tasks. They need to check the readiness of nodes, either without or with CNI. For Task 9, I\'ll use wait_for with path /healthz, expecting a 200 status. For Task 10, I\'ll use wait_for with /ready and a 200 status. Both have retries=60 and delay=10. The until section uses shell commands to check kubectl get nodes and ensure they\'re ready.\n\nI need to make sure all tasks are correctly ordered and that variables are properly referenced. Also, I should ensure that the YAML is valid, using proper indentation and structure without any comments or extra lines. Each task should be a separate entry under the tasks list, using the correct module names and parameters.\n\nI think I\'ve covered all the tasks and their descriptions. Now, I\'ll structure the playbook with each task as described, making sure to include all necessary modules, variables, and notifications where required. I\'ll double-check the YAML syntax to avoid any linting errors and ensure it fits within an Ansible Role\'s tasks directory.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create the RKE2 config directory\n  file:\n    path: /etc/rke2\n    state: directory\n\n- name: Set server taints\n  shell: kubectl taint nodes --all node-role.kubernetes.io/{{ rke2_type }}=true:NoSchedule\n  when: rke2_type == \'server\'\n\n- name: Set agent taints\n  shell: kubectl taint nodes --all node-role.kubernetes.io/{{ rke2_type }}=true:NoSchedule\n  when: rke2_type == \'agent\'\n\n- name: Copy RKE2 config file\n  copy:\n    remote_src: yes\n    src: config.yaml\n    dest: /etc/rke2/config.yaml\n  notify: rke2_config_handler\n\n- name: Copy kubelet config file\n  copy:\n    remote_src: yes\n    src: kubelet.yaml\n    dest: /etc/rke2/kubelet.yaml\n  when: rke2_kubelet_config is not empty\n  notify: rke2_config_handler\n\n- name: Copy Containerd Registry Configuration file\n  copy:\n    remote_src: yes\n    src: containerd-registry-config.json\n    dest: /etc/containerd/registry.json\n  when: rke2_containerd_config is not empty\n  notify: rke2_containerd_handler\n\n- name: Start RKE2 service\n  shell: systemctl start rke2\n  args:\n    chdir: /etc/rke2\n  register: rke2_start\n  until: rke2_start | success\n  retries: 3\n  delay: 10\n  notify: rke2_service_handler\n\n- name: Mask other RKE2 services\n  shell: systemctl mask rke2\n  when: rke2_type != \'server\'\n\n- name: Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - no CNI\n  wait_for:\n    path: /healthz\n    state: started\n    http_status: 200\n  retries: 60\n  delay: 10\n  until: kubectl get nodes | grep -v NotReady | wc -l | { read num; echo "$num"; } | until num == total_nodes\n\n- name: Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - with CNI\n  wait_for:\n    path: /ready\n    state: started\n    http_status: 200\n  retries: 60\n  delay: 10\n  until: kubectl get nodes -o=jsonpath=\'{range .items[*]}{.status.conditions[?(@.type=="Ready")].status}{", "}{.status.phase}{", "}\' | grep -q "True, Ready"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T07:57:18.482511002Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 21655966707, 'load_duration': 2646598731, 'prompt_eval_count': 599, 'prompt_eval_duration': 395404943, 'eval_count': 1323, 'eval_duration': 18612941456, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--e4f44ea5-6bc3-453a-878a-33ef1be4a1c4-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 599, 'output_tokens': 1323, 'total_tokens': 1922}
