content='<think>\nAlright, I need to fix the Ansible Playbook so that it passes ansible-lint. Let\'s look at the error messages to understand what\'s wrong.\n\nFirst, there are issues with the `mode: 755` being a risky octal literal. Ansible-lint prefers using symbolic modes or leading zeros. So, I should change `755` to `0o755` or use symbolic like `mode: \'01363\'`. But since the user didn\'t specify, I\'ll go with `0o755` for clarity.\n\nNext, the FQCN (Fully Qualified Class Name) errors. The modules `file` and `template` are being used without their full names. Ansible now prefers `ansible.builtin.file` and `ansible.builtin.template` instead of just `file` or `template`. I\'ll update the module names accordingly.\n\nLooking at each task:\n\n1. **Create the RKE2 manifests directory**: The module is `file`, which should be `ansible.builtin.file`. Also, the `mode` is `755`, so I\'ll change that to `0o755`.\n\n2. **Copy kube-vip files**: The module is `template`, so I\'ll change it to `ansible.builtin.template`. The `mode` needs updating to `0o755` as well.\n\n3. **Copy load balancer manifests**: Same as above, update the module to `ansible.builtin.template` and `mode` to `0o755`.\n\nI also need to ensure that the `when` condition uses the correct variable. In Ansible, it\'s `ansible_cloud_provider_enabled` or similar, but the original uses `cloud_provider is enabled`, so I\'ll leave that as is unless instructed otherwise.\n\nNo other tasks or variables are to be altered. I\'ll make sure the YAML structure is correct, with proper indentation and syntax.\n\nNow, I\'ll rewrite each task with these fixes, keeping the rest of the structure intact.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create the RKE2 manifests directory\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /etc/rke2/manifests\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0o755\n\n- name: Copy kube-vip files to first server\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: "{{ item }}"\n    dest: /etc/rke2/manifests/\n    mode: 0o755\n  with_items:\n    "{{ lookup(\'ansible.builtin.file\', \'files/kube-vip/*.yaml.j2\') | list }}"\n  register: kubevip_files\n\n- name: Copy kube-vip load balancer manifests to first server\n  when: cloud_provider is enabled\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: "{{ item }}"\n    dest: /etc/rke2/manifests/\n    mode: 0o755\n  with_items:\n    "{{ lookup(\'ansible.builtin.file\', \'files/kube-vip/loadbalancer-*.yaml.j2\') | list }}"\n  register: kubevip_loadbalancer\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-08T08:07:37.819537429Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 16566815134, 'load_duration': 89487298, 'prompt_eval_count': 2165, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1549128892, 'eval_count': 650, 'eval_duration': 14926246061, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--f668a3fc-1f7a-4836-917f-6cee157fd688-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2165, 'output_tokens': 650, 'total_tokens': 2815}
