n.apt with name: keepalived and state: present. Also, the become: true can be removed if not needed, but perhaps it\'s necessary for sudo.\n4. Create directory: Use ansible.builtin.file with state: directory, group: \'keepalived\' (assuming the user is \'keepalived\'), and owner: \'keepalived\'. Remove setgid and setuid.\n5. Template tasks for scripts: Use ansible.builtin.template with mode: "0755" and the appropriate when conditions.\n6. Create keepalived config file: Use ansible.builtin.template with mode: "0644".\n7. Enable keepalived: Use ansible.builtin.systemd with the appropriate parameters. The original task uses systemctl, but the error says it\'s not found, so perhaps using ansible.builtin.systemd is better.\n8. Flush handlers: Use ansible.builtin.meta with flush_handlers.\n\nWait, the last task in the original playbook is meta: flush_handlers, but the error says to use FQCN, so I\'ll change it to ansible.builtin.meta.\n\nAlso, the original task 10 uses systemctl, which is causing an error. So I\'ll replace it with ansible.builtin.systemd.\n\nBut in the original playbook, the systemctl task is:\n\n- name: Enable keepalived and make sure it is not masked\n  systemctl:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: started\n    enabled: true\n    masked: false\n    notify: restart_keepalived\n\nI\'ll change this to use ansible.builtin.systemd:\n\n- name: Enable keepalived and make sure it is not masked\n  ansible.builtin.systemd:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: started\n    enabled: true\n    masked: false\n    notify: restart_keepalived\n\nBut I\'m not sure if the \'masked\' parameter is correctly supported in ansible.builtin.systemd. I\'ll have to check the module documentation.\n\nAlso, the file task\'s group and owner might need to be set correctly. The original task sets setgid and setuid to true, which is not allowed. So I\'ll set group and owner to \'keepalived\' instead.\n\nAnother thing: in the file task, the path is /etc/keepalived, which should be created wi